From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: CanConvert to the wide formats did not crash (6049)

WICConvertBitmapSource and IWICFormatConverter::CanConvert to 64bppPRGBA,
64bppRGBAHalf, 64bppPRGBAHalf and the 128bpp float formats crashed:
CanConvert tries the destination's copy function with no rectangle on a
converter not yet initialized, and copypixels_wide read the converter's
destination format first. It answers S_OK with no rectangle, as the other
copy functions do.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windowscodecs/converter.c b/dlls/windowscodecs/converter.c
index f2046cb..ede3e83 100644
--- a/dlls/windowscodecs/converter.c
+++ b/dlls/windowscodecs/converter.c
@@ -2112,6 +2112,11 @@ static BOOL wide_dest_is_direct(enum pixelformat dst)
 static HRESULT copypixels_wide(struct FormatConverter *This, const WICRect *prc,
     UINT cbStride, UINT cbBufferSize, BYTE *pbBuffer, enum pixelformat source_format)
 {
+    /* CanConvert asks with no rectangle, before Initialize has set a destination */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_WIC_WIDE_CANCONVERT
+    if (!prc)
+        return S_OK;
+#endif
     return convert_wide(This, prc, cbStride, cbBufferSize, pbBuffer, source_format,
             This->dst_format->format);
 }
